{"name":"Glacier Lake","hex":"#62b4c0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glacier","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of ice which flows under its own mass, usually downhill.","An area of a mountain where snow is present year-round."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glacier"},{"term":"lake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, landlocked stretch of water or similar liquid.","A large amount of liquid."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An offering, sacrifice, gift.","Play; sport; game; fun; glee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glacier Lake (Alberta)","blocks":[{"text":"Glacier Lake is the fourth largest lake in Banff National Park, in Alberta, Canada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/A_Calm_Morninf_at_Glacier_Lake.jpg/330px-A_Calm_Morninf_at_Glacier_Lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glacier_Lake_(Alberta)","wikidata":"Q22645992"},{"title":"Glacier Lake (Custer County, Idaho)","blocks":[{"text":"Glacier Lake is an alpine lake in Custer County, Idaho, United States, located in the White Cloud Mountains in the Sawtooth National Recreation Area. While no trails lead to the lake, it can be accessed from Sawtooth National Forest trail 047."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glacier_Lake_(Custer_County%2C_Idaho)","wikidata":"Q5566140"},{"title":"Glacier Lake (Washington)","blocks":[{"text":"Glacier Lake is a small alpine freshwater lake located on the northern skirt of Chikamin Peak and Lemah Mountain in Kittitas County, Washington. Because of its proximity to surrounding peaks and mountains at the heart of the Alpine Lakes Wilderness, the lake is a popular area for hiking, camping, and fishing golden trout. Glacier Lake is a short distance between Chikamin Lake and Spectacle Lake at the base of Chikamin Ridge. The Pacific Crest Trail is a short distance from Glacier Lake as well as other Alpine lakes located in the vicinity. To the North is Avalanche Lake and Iceberg Lake at the base of Lemah Mountain."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glacier_Lake_(Washington)","wikidata":"Q49302568"},{"title":"Glacial lake","blocks":[{"text":"A glacial lake is a body of water with origins from glacier activity. They are formed when a glacier erodes the land and then melts, filling the depression created by the glacier."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Great_Lakes_from_space.jpg/330px-Great_Lakes_from_space.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glacial_lake","wikidata":"Q211302"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Glacier_Lake_in_Banff_National_Park.jpg/500px-Glacier_Lake_in_Banff_National_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Glacier_Lake_in_Banff_National_Park.jpg/1280px-Glacier_Lake_in_Banff_National_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Glacier_Lake_in_Banff_National_Park.jpg/500px-Glacier_Lake_in_Banff_National_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Glacier Lake (centered) seen from Mt. Sarbach. Mt Outram to far left, Division Mountain and Lyell Glacier in back, Mount Erasmus to right, and Howse River across bottom of frame.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlacier_Lake_in_Banff_National_Park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Agassiz.jpg/500px-Agassiz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Agassiz.jpg/1280px-Agassiz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped